# Supabase migrations

- **Don't edit a migration that was already applied on staging or production.** They are read-only.
- To change something from a past migration, add a **new** migration.
- Only migrations that were not applied yet are created or edited.
- Never run `supabase db push`: the CI `deploy-migrations` job applies migrations to `plant-staging` after a merge to `staging` and Tomas's approval (see `CLAUDE.md`). Until the beta that database is also production's, so migrations are additive only (see `CLAUDE.md`).
- Every new migration passes squawk and starts with the header in `scripts/fixtures/squawk/pass-migration-header.sql`, except a lone `... INDEX CONCURRENTLY` statement (see `CLAUDE.md`).
- Every table is born with RLS (`user_id = (select auth.uid())` in `USING` and `WITH CHECK`) and an explicit `GRANT` to `authenticated`, never to `anon`. The global reference tables `fx_rates`, `prices` and `instruments` are the only ones without `user_id` (read-only for `authenticated`, see `CLAUDE.md`). Every `public` table also gets the RESTRICTIVE MFA gate, copied from the house form in `.agents/skills/enforce-owner-isolation/SKILL.md` (the pgTAP floor compares its text).
